gion $D$ shown above. If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+xy & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${∬}_{R}({x}^{2}+xy)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[0,2]\\times [-1,1]$\n- ${∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+xy)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[0,2]\\times [-2,2]$\n- ${∬}_{R}({x}^{2}+xy)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[0,3]\\times [-2,2]$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Notice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+xy, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain \n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+xy)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The rectangle $R$ does not cover the region $D.$ Also, the integrals have not been stated correctly with respect to the domains $R$ and $D$ (they have been swapped).\n\n- Statement II is true. The rectangle $R$ covers the region $D$ completely.\n\n- Statement III is false. The integrals have not been stated correctly with respect to the domains $R$ and $D$ (they have been swapped).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348413 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152200 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "100ab73e-3dad-5b15-9da2-d244c67bcc9b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Double Integrals Over Non-Rectangular Domains" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049229 :topic/id #uuid "e52ab899-5fcb-50d2-afee-4830a70f16df" :topic/math-academy-id 2616 :topic/title "Double Integrals Over Non-Rectangular Domains"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9cac20f8-0c6e-5c22-96f1-a90b74e7288e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 