7592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "45255a84-5494-574a-bd9f-880b4b37a48c" :question/math-academy-id "q-80669" :question/problem "Determine the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+3x}{{x}^{2}-3x-4}.$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.\n\n- **I.** $x=-3$\n- **II.** $x=-1$\n- **III.** $x=0$\n- **IV.** $x=4$" :question/worked-solution "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nFactoring the numerator and denominator, we get\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{x(x+3)}{(x+1)(x-4)}.\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)(x-4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the two solutions $x=-1$ and $x=4.$ Therefore, the equations of the vertical asymptotes are $x=-1$ and $x=4.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348434 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087844 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b18ace11-d31c-5d5a-bd2e-32e1c28af2b9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Vertical Asymptotes When the Denominator Has Complex Roots" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049363 :topic/id #uuid "eefd5285-6b99-569d-a5bb-365f176fa757" :topic/math-academy-id 807 :topic/title "Vertical Asymptotes of Rational Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38427c47-6a48-59eb-baae-0cd579cf066e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439969} {:answer/id #uuid "f23fff08-7ea9-52a7-9e88-f5a94698619b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439970}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38427c47-6a48-59eb-baae-0cd579cf066e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439969} :answer-field/id #uuid "1911fc60-54f6-517c-8ae8-21b2ce16ca8c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440342} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5572999-573e-529b-862f-4bb6987d4a08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439971} {:answer/id #uuid "4337c38c-3dfe-5b58-916f-32783c4bed89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439972}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5572999-573e-529b-862f-4bb6987d4a08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439971} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc150f73-610e-51a3-838e-ff730a027cbf" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440343} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "febf4efe-8826-5f6a-9c5e-0d33123893e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439973} {:answer/id #uuid "e201d944-0761-5a84-9e70-3abd37d71214" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439974}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e201d944-0761-5a84-9e70-3abd37d71214" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439974} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9575f0f-78af-5d52-b5a5-b76147fe2120" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440344}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6e336039-4f92-550b-b76c-a2a62662e884" :question/math-academy-id "q-80676" :question/problem "Calculate the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{2x-1}{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+4x-8}.$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.\n\n- **I.** $x=-2$\n- **II.** $x=0$\n- **III.** $x=2$" :question/worked-solution "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nFactoring the numerator and denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{2x-1}{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+4x-8} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x-1}{{x}^{2}(x-2)+4(x-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x-1}{({x}^{2}+4)(x-2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the denominator equal to zero. This gives\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+4)(x-2)=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve the above equation using the zero product property:\n\n- Solving $x-2=0$ gives the solution $x=2.$\n\n- The equation ${x}^{2}+4=0$ has no real solutions.\n\nTherefore, the only vertical asymptote is $x=2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348436 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087843 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "53b26ee4-53af-5660-a9e6-8e5cca8b3e1d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Vertical Asymptotes With Common Factors in the Numerator and Denominator" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049363 :topic/id #uuid "eefd5285-6b99-569d-a5bb-365f176fa757" :topic/math-academy-id 807 :topic/title "Vertical Asymptotes of Rational Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17477df2-f0f4-5538-a244-56aea05cba72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439987} {:answer/id #uuid "4111ff3c-d0bc-54cd-ae53-5033ced42cf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 1