58} {:answer/id #uuid "352bc0a4-63f3-533a-9169-0c4e8caf6d0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469259}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "352bc0a4-63f3-533a-9169-0c4e8caf6d0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469259} :answer-field/id #uuid "5df64f49-e9ef-59e7-bddf-ece87e1d372c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470241}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "231d9a8a-12f5-5ef7-842a-1be3e946bcb6" :question/math-academy-id "q-81816" :question/problem "A triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-3,0),(1,5),(2,-2).$  Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the **clockwise** rotation ${R}_{-{180}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${180}^{∘}$ about the origin?\n- **I.** $(-2,2)$\n- **II.** $(0,3)$\n- **III.** $(-1,-5)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The clockwise rotation ${R}_{-{180}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${180}^{∘}$ is the same as counterclockwise rotation by the same angle. It's given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{-{180}^{∘}},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{-{180}^{∘}}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(3,0),(-1,-5),(-2,2).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351374 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092224 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "20f4ef93-3e7b-58ec-992e-3a62b12b74e2" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Matrix That Represents a Rotation of 180 Degrees" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048712 :topic/id #uuid "b784cbd9-6f0d-5689-9a0e-6e19dfca34c7" :topic/math-academy-id 931 :topic/title "Right-Angle Rotations as Linear Transformations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bdcbfd3a-e8a0-5cc7-b990-7a59096f3316" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469260} {:answer/id #uuid "a1b17aa7-7706-56e2-9568-216559170626" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469261}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bdcbfd3a-e8a0-5cc7-b990-7a59096f3316" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469260} :answer-field/id #uuid "689e532d-e49f-5735-95f4-265640006f3c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470242} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7acdb258-0684-5d30-b56c-6a89b7f37228" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469262} {:answer/id #uuid "39d59cfc-e8e1-5e07-afed-229e5ae564f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469263}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39d59cfc-e8e1-5e07-afed-229e5ae564f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469263} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0bb51e3-3579-5cb4-93d0-8300ee25ac9b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470243} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ebaf7ae-85f0-55f4-a9ca-7504d60594c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469264} {:answer/id #uuid "83eae6a6-2a8e-5c81-beb6-b9af6cd108b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469265}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ebaf7ae-85f0-55f4-a9ca-7504d60594c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469264} :answer-field/id #uuid "f211414f-b39b-585b-b430-bb13e3714449" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470244}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cedf0fcc-98d4-596a-ad79-42e7fd62dfba" :question/math-academy-id "q-81818" :question/problem "A triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-5,1),(0,-4),(3,5).$  Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{\\pi }$ by an angle of $\\pi $ radians about the origin?\n- **I.** $(4,0)$\n- **II.** $(-3,-5)$\n- **III.** $(-1,5)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{\\pi }$ by an angle of $\\pi $ radians is given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{\\pi },$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{\\pi }$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(5,-1),(0,4),(-3,-5).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351375 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092224 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "20f4ef93-3e7b-58ec-992e-3a62b12b74e2" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Matrix That Represents a Rotation of 180 Degrees" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048712 :topic/id #uuid "b784cbd9-6f0d-5689-9a0e-6e19dfca34c7" :topic/math-academy-id 931 :topic/title "Right-Angle Rotations as Linear Transformations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1dc15f59-c768-5320-9ec4-70f3d142b675" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469266} {:answer/id #uuid "5187f972-9f94-5165-af76-273d295ea3ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469267}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1dc15f59-c768-5320-9ec4-70f3d142b675" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469266} :answer-field/id #uuid "dfe89ca2-2337-508f-92ae-92b8182116cc" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470245} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7897b954-a80d-5552-9b97-0e5fbd8e14e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469268} {:answer/id #uuid "fbd275cb-adea-5351-8c2d-fe4629e73b90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469269}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fbd275cb-adea-5351-8c2d-fe4629e73b90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469269} :answer-field/id #uuid "90f7b91a-9437-57e9-a79f-e0b93efe37d8" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470246} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "837117d8-f384-5bd9-a6ce-cc9066fb6bb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469270} {:answer/id #uuid "12466bb5-6322-58ca-959d-97ddedf72119" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469271}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12466bb5-6322-58ca-959d-97ddedf72119" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469271} :answer-field/id #uuid "c16860bd-48c3-55ea-a6e4-2951ea1c0825" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470247}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "eca92846-b208-5714-9d9f-4947d539dbcc" :question/math-academy-id "q-81819" :question/problem "A triangle $S$ has vertices at $(4,4),(-3,-3),(-1,7).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{{180}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${180}^{∘}$ about the origin?\n- **I.** $(3,-3)$\n- **II.** $(-4,-4)$\n- **III.** $(1,-7)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{{180}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${180}^{∘}$ is given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{{180}^{∘}},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{{180}^{∘}}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-4,-4),(3,3),(1,-7).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351410 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133913 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abaeea03-6a2a-5d37-a2af-a9ea109175ad" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reasons Why a Determinant Equals Zero" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049312 :topic/id #uuid "eb826c2f-ae04-5de5-b6a6-7efcf7e974ae" :topic/math-academy-id 2201 :topic/title "Conditions When a Determinant Equals Zero"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87131d2a-00fa-5c86-adb5-5dcd9781663d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451839} {:answer/id #uuid "c5992e5f-0eac-5510-8b9e-4c9bdb590e1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451840}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5992e5f-0eac-5510-8b9e-4c9bdb590e1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451840} :answer-field/id #uuid "f556a776-7b3e-5b87-96a3-38f6c6a85224" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452767} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94e1abfb-4ac1-5387-8365-44f8be67855e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451841} {:answer/id #uuid "1ae75960-5f9e-5be6-9aa4-ca852b78c6e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451842}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94e1abfb-4ac1-5387-8365-44f8be67855e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451841} :answer-field/id #uuid "4203a946-5791-54e5-8948-df9e4bceec16" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452768} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3316e667-7cb8-5d37-8ca1-05b94216632d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451843} {:answer/id #uuid "e4ec2c90-b24e-58ba-a3ab-9443e572892a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451844}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3316e667-7cb8-5d37-8ca1-05b94216632d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451843} :answer-field/id #uuid "038959f0-30da-57d8-900b-1c0a7eef35de" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452769}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e8066ca0-5e8f-5876-924e-8be55bf1f74e" :question/math-academy-id "q-82290" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix such that $|A|=0.$ Which of the following statements must be true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** One of the rows/columns of $A$ is proportional to another row/column of $A$\n- **II.** $A$ has two identical rows\n- **III.** $A$ has a zero row" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, we can make use of the following fact:\n\n$|A|=0$ *if and only if one of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A.$*\n\nIn the case of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, this means that one of the rows/columns must be proportional to another row/column.\n\n- Statements II and III are false. For example, consider the matrix \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWe have that \n\n$$\n|A|=4\\cdot 3-6\\cdot 2=0\n$$\n\nbut $A$ has neither two identical rows nor a zero row.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351421 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133843 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee1838df-f1d6-5bc4-908c-b96e2ad577c9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Sets are Orthogonal" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049811 :topic/id #uuid "157ebcd0-6389-529a-a695-53136d4482c5" :topic/math-academy-id 2103 :topic/title "Orthogonal Sets in Euclidean Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eec7f9d0-6840-5a0d-9763-9d79e17c960b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469272} {:answer/id #uuid "e17563c3-bef4-5de4-bfa8-3abc6787cdbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469273}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eec7f9d0-6840-5a0d-9763-9d79e17c960b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469272} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2536c2a-97f0-5d07-85f7-dac71d9a3595" :answer-field/key "U" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17