d/id #uuid "790adcf9-f3da-50a3-aa5c-dce48917f693" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470262}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5104f251-39bc-5c29-bbcf-96e73f6b8fe5" :question/math-academy-id "q-8297" :question/problem "Let \n$T:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}3y \\\\ 2x\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $T(kv)=kT(v)$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vector $v$ and real scalar $k$\n- **II.** $T({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})=T({v}_{1})+T({v}_{2})$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$\n- **III.** $T$ is a linear transformation\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A linear transformation $T$ satisfies two properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & T\\begin{bmatrix}kx \\\\ ky\\end{bmatrix}=kT\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}, \\\\  & T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the first condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\begin{bmatrix}kx \\\\ ky\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3ky \\\\ 2kx\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =k\\begin{bmatrix}3y \\\\ 2x\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =kT\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the second condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3({y}_{1}+{y}_{2}) \\\\ 2({x}_{1}+{x}_{2})\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3{y}_{1} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3{y}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{T}$ is a linear transformation.\n\nAs a result, all three statements are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351535 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133843 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee1838df-f1d6-5bc4-908c-b96e2ad577c9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Sets are Orthogonal" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049811 :topic/id #uuid "157ebcd0-6389-529a-a695-53136d4482c5" :topic/math-academy-id 2103 :topic/title "Orthogonal Sets in Euclidean Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c093387-dd3a-57fc-9e3f-4c7d701bbf43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469308} {:answer/id #uuid "176aa2ed-e6ac-570d-9901-4a949990fefc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469309}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "176aa2ed-e6ac-570d-9901-4a949990fefc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469309} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf0364b8-59fa-5366-a895-e2c63cf5360e" :answer-field/key "U" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470266} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f17293f1-9f27-550b-852c-f9600bba572e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469310} {:answer/id #uuid "cb40de30-bab0-5067-aa1b-eaab8f18473e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469311}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f17293f1-9f27-550b-852c-f9600bba572e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469310} :answer-field/id #uuid "70354c98-f319-582a-83ff-19758bae87e9" :answer-field/key "V" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470267} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5a9e39c-cf8a-532c-8d40-ac1ef810c40c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469312} {:answer/id #uuid "7ff70d68-31cf-5e99-9978-28a69b4ad0a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ff70d68-31cf-5e99-9978-28a69b4ad0a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469313} :answer-field/id #uuid "31ee54a9-4b1b-5582-ab2f-d95c19306c24" :answer-field/key "W" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470268}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3593d781-0056-56f1-8b48-1ee74f8fd0fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-83719" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are orthogonal?\n- **U.** $U={\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}$\n- **V.** $V={\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}}$\n- **W.** $W={\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of the given sets as \n${{u}_{1},{u}_{2},{u}_{3}},$ \n${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}},$ and \n${{w}_{1},{w}_{2}},$ respectively. \n\nThe sets $U,V,$ and $W$ are orthogonal if the following conditions on each set hold:\n\n- ${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0,\\,{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{3}=0,\\,{u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{3}=0.$\n\n- ${v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2}=0,\\,{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{3}=0,\\,{v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{3}=0.$\n\n- ${w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2}=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- For the set $U,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=-1+0+1=0 & ✓ \\\\ {u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{3} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=0+0+0=0 & ✓ \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{3} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=0+0+0=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the set $U$ is orthogonal.\n\n- For the set $V,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}=12+0+1=13\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $V$ is not an orthogonal set.\n\n- For the set $W,$ notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}=-40+40=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the set $W$ is orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"$U$ and $W$ only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351542 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133781 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ed5c8af7-e617-5e8c-be01-45a26eb17d4d" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Sets are Orthonormal" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049811 :topic/id #uuid "157ebcd0-6389-529a-a695-53136d4482c5" :topic/math-academy-id 2103 :topic/title "Orthogonal Sets in Euclidean Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca53a596-697d-5074-8ae7-cadb576b9f33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469314} {:answer/id #uuid "9028cf1d-3482-555c-9254-f303dd967e7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469315}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9028cf1d-3482-555c-9254-f303dd967e7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469315} :answer-field/id #uuid "52cd5a79-76c1-53fd-98ef-78fe65d3a648" :answer-field/key "U" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470269} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a455406-0fed-5b3e-86c0-bc18ad51b9f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469316} {:answer/id #uuid "9e86cc99-94e1-57ad-bf00-0827b339489c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a455406-0fed-5b3e-86c0-bc18ad51b9f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469316} :answer-field/id #uuid "80e1d8bc-8a01-5f07-a31e-e1514db3104e" :answer-field/key "V" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470270} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45a09ee1-e29a-5fb9-b33d-83923959cc1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469318} {:answer/id #uuid "a77d1b68-ce1e-502a-b145-e7f6e0d90c36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469319}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a77d1b68-ce1e-502a-b145-e7f6e0d90c36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469319} :answer-field/id #uuid "2991993f-85de-54a4-8a97-c77e6abc7b72" :answer-field/key "W" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470271}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "757ea74d-034b-5cf5-b116-1f66ebbe72c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-83745" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are orthonormal?\n- **U.** $U={\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}}$\n- **V.** $V={\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}}$\n- **W.** $W={\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of the given sets as \n${{u}_{1},{u}_{2}},$ \n${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}},$ and \n${{w}_{1},{w}_{2}},$ respectively. \n\nThe sets $U,V,$ and $W$ are orthonormal if the following conditions on each set hold:\n\n- ${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0\\,\\text{and}\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{1} &=1 \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{2} &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.$\n\n- $\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2} &=0 \\\\ {v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{3} &=0 \\\\ {v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{3} &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\text{and}\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1} &=1 \\\\ {v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2} &=1 \\\\ {v}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3} &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.$\n\n- ${w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2}=0\\,\\text{and}\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{1} &=1 \\\\ {w}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{2} &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- For the set $U,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}=-\\frac{6}{13}+\\frac{6}{13}=0 & ✓ \\\\ {u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{4}{13}+\\frac{9}{13}=1 & ✓ \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{9}{13}+\\frac{4}{13}=1 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the set $U$ is orthonormal.\n\n- For the set $V,$ notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}=0+1+8=9\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $V$ is not an orthonormal set.\n\n- For the set $W,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{2}{5}-\\frac{2}{5}=0 & ✓ \\\\ {w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{4}{5}+\\frac{1}{5}=1 & ✓ \\\\ {w}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{4}{5}=1 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $W$ is an orthonormal set.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"$U$ and $W$ only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351543 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105817 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f7256c7-afea-5c33-a859-623b0531e88c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Discrete Random Variables" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048368 :topic/id #uuid "99cc78ff-5612-5e6a-a347-8c2389044b69" :topic/math-academy-id 1290 :topic/title "Probability Mass Functions of Discrete Random Variables"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4297ecbb-b0ee-5dc0-bd63-d03e3130f18e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469320} {:answer/id #uuid "63d17ef6-dadc-5555-9854-793b7015eb88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469321}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4297ecbb-b0ee-5dc0-bd63-d03e3130f18e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469320} :answer-field/id #uuid "7cc036fb-c682-5f64-bdcb-62dd0b682889" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470272} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93381047-9ed8-5484-93f2-25c7f4c5fa70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469322} {:answer/id #uuid "9208c164-d449-59c9-8092-37d004d5cf0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469323}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9208c164-d449-59c9-8092-37d004d5cf0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469323} :answer-field/id #uuid "28beabc5-8df4-5765-86e5-a44704b8af19" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470273} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e30d3efb-fd0f-5566-9694-0f017625f10b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469324} {:answer/id #uuid "8b87ef0b-9201-5bf1-909e-8cf4bdeb334f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469325}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b87ef0b-9201-5bf1-909e-8cf4bdeb334f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469325} :answer-field/id #uuid "a86472cb-dccb-505a-8cc8-64e34848e136" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470274}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "97ab1308-2ae6-5488-8b7b-f352f2f86ff6" :question/math-academy-id "q-83746" :question/problem "Which of the following are discrete random variables?\n- **I.** The number of hearts in a standard deck of cards\n- **II.** The number of diamonds obtained when $7$ cards are randomly selected from a standard deck of cards\n- **III.** The number of times a card is selected from a standard deck of cards until a King appears\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A random variable is a variable whose value is determined by the outcome of a trial or experiment.\n\nA *discrete* random variable is a random variable\n\n- that has finitely many possible values, or\n\n- whose possible values can be listed in a sequence: ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3},…$\n\nRemember that a real interval (e.g. $(a,b)$ or $[a,b]$) cannot be listed in a sequence.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I does *not* describe a discrete random variable. The number of hearts in a particular complete deck of cards is not the outcome of a trial or experiment.\n\n- Statement II describes a discrete random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, and its possible values can be listed in a sequence: $0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7.$\n\n- Statement III describes a discrete random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, and we can count its possible values in a sequence: $1,2,3,…$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351546 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105817 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f7256c7-afea-5c33-a859-623b0531e88c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Discrete Random Variables" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048368 :topic/id #uuid "99cc78ff-5612-5e6a-a347-8c2389044b69" :topic/math-academy-id 1290 :topic/title "Probability Mass Functions of Discrete Random Variables"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a33bf7f-eb87-5aa4-9136-66daeb8919e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469326} {:answer/id #uuid "e4a78649-601b-5451-91a3-23db522dd24b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a33bf7f-eb87-5aa4-9136-66daeb8919e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469326} :answer-field/id #uuid "6718d775-0414-5022-9f48-edef5cf16d5d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470275} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7eee3bc-a0bb-518f-a7a2-784cb9c38fcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469328} {:answer/id #uuid "88bd7805-e700-57ce-8216-0d9a8a36fbc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469329}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88bd7805-e700-57ce-8216-0d