#edb/ref 17592186469348} {:answer/id #uuid "81a7ba05-ee60-58cd-a5a6-e1046165b2a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43e0892a-70ad-5bf8-a99c-fd5c6d0c1379" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469348} :answer-field/id #uuid "81d9abd9-b8ca-5470-8dbb-280bbbd3ab7b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470286}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0d05b255-e15a-5a84-a441-46629f916127" :question/math-academy-id "q-8394" :question/problem "A triangle $S$ has vertices at $(0,0),(1,5),(2,3).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{\\pi /2}$ by an angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ radians about the origin?\n- **I.** $(-5,1)$\n- **II.** $(0,-2)$\n- **III.** $(2,-3)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{\\pi /2}$ by an angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ radians is given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{\\pi /2},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{\\pi /2}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -5 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(0,0),(-5,1),(-3,2).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354272 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092223 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b86558a-4c99-5ccb-a100-719692a056f4" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Matrix That Represents a Rotation of 90 Degrees" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048712 :topic/id #uuid "b784cbd9-6f0d-5689-9a0e-6e19dfca34c7" :topic/math-academy-id 931 :topic/title "Right-Angle Rotations as Linear Transformations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3d3e243-980a-5443-b39f-968258eea1dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469350} {:answer/id #uuid "b293378d-5abc-5d1a-95f9-ffaf61440ffb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469351}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b293378d-5abc-5d1a-95f9-ffaf61440ffb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469351} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8a6f178-1ec1-54b0-8ab8-948072730c0e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470287} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "521c8f26-598c-5fe9-9ae9-e0dbe28c2a36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469352} {:answer/id #uuid "0b1b5eaa-2de3-5c59-8e59-a21eb831a1a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469353}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b1b5eaa-2de3-5c59-8e59-a21eb831a1a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469353} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d28f5b1-d171-5151-ae2d-cabe08dd66c3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470288} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66b67f71-bc1d-57b3-9bb7-f4588496d4fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469354} {:answer/id #uuid "52838fcf-c810-505d-9410-f0a6baa70168" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469355}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52838fcf-c810-505d-9410-f0a6baa70168" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469355} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2b19c0e-27eb-57f4-bdae-6187dc80479f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470289}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3264cc98-99b3-5ee3-bfae-d22a0332c3e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-8395" :question/problem "A triangle $S$ has vertices at  $(0,2),(3,0),(0,0).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the **clockwise** rotation ${R}_{-{90}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${90}^{∘}$ about the origin?\n- **I.** $(0,-3)$\n- **II.** $(0,0)$\n- **III.** $(2,0)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The clockwise rotation ${R}_{-{90}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${90}^{∘}$ is the same as counterclockwise rotation by an angle of ${270}^{∘}.$ It's given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{-{90}^{∘}},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{-{90}^{∘}}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(2,0),(0,-3),(0,0).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354275 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092224 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "20f4ef93-3e7b-58ec-992e-3a62b12b74e2" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Matrix That Represents a Rotation of 180 Degrees" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048712 :topic/id #uuid "b784cbd9-6f0d-5689-9a0e-6e19dfca34c7" :topic/math-academy-id 931 :topic/title "Right-Angle Rotations as Linear Transformations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "713bf4d1-ab25-5361-9e9c-7d24f6109f86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469356} {:answer/id #uuid "fca5df3a-3e5a-5e39-9a04-d3f319e7d84e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fca5df3a-3e5a-5e39-9a04-d3f319e7d84e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469357} :answer-field/id #uuid "00bfb755-07a7-5384-afe7-6f942d8cdae4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470290} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cedc26c-1cb4-5561-91be-d73dca72eab2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469358} {:answer/id #uuid "5c31dbde-32b2-5234-9bd4-6944f689fadc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 175921860